  "name": "@iswangwenbin/promptx-mcp-server",
  "readme": "# @iswangwenbin/promptx-mcp-server\n\nPromptX MCP server for Claude, Codex, Cursor, and other MCP-compatible clients.\n\n## Install and run\n\n```bash\nnpx -y @iswangwenbin/promptx-mcp-server\n```\n\nVerify the installed version:\n\n```bash\nnpx -y @iswangwenbin/promptx-mcp-server --version\n```\n\nThe current published version is `2.4.3`.\n\n## Client configuration\n\n```json\n{\n  \"mcpServers\": {\n    \"promptx\": {\n      \"command\": \"npx\",\n      \"args\": [\"-y\", \"@iswangwenbin/promptx-mcp-server\"]\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nFor Codex on Windows, use `cmd.exe` as the shell shim:\n\n```toml\n[mcp_servers.promptx]\ncommand = \"cmd.exe\"\nargs = [\"/c\", \"npx\", \"-y\", \"@iswangwenbin/promptx-mcp-server\"]\nenv = { SystemRoot = \"C:\\\\Windows\" }\nstartup_timeout_ms = 120000\n```\n\nThe package exposes both `promptx-mcp-server` and `mcp-server` command names.\n",
  "readmeFilename": "README.md",
